 "post_hoc_reading_added_after_run": {
  "HR_S_per_unit_above_[2,20]": "Cox HR per unit of S = 36.725 [19.813, 68.072] exceeds the pre-registered per-unit ceiling of 20. The per-unit figure extrapolates over 1/0.186 = 5.4 standard deviations of S (SD 0.186 in sample A); the per-SD HR, 1.96 [1.74, 2.19], is inside its pre-registered range [1.3, 2.5], the permuted-S HR interval covers 1 (1.22 [0.68, 2.21]), the synthetic known-answer recovers HR 4 on both paths (4.29 Cox, 4.25 cloglog), and the early-vs-never AUC reproduces the published 0.78 (0.793). The per-unit ceiling was mis-calibrated for a covariate with SD 0.19, not a pipeline fault. The two estimation paths differ (Cox-Efron 36.7 vs cloglog 50.9): 159 of 324 events are tied at T = 0 (33% of the initial risk set), where the Efron approximation attenuates; the grouped-time cloglog is the model matched to report-year data. Headline to report: HR per SD of S and the Kaplan–Meier disposal shares by signal tercile (year 1: 0.24 / 0.54 / 0.74; year 5: 0.39 / 0.82 / 0.85).",
  "time_variation": "Expected a front-loaded S effect; found a front-loaded BASELINE hazard (0.21, 0.21, 0.14, 0.10, 0.10, 0.065 by duration year at covariate means) with a stable S gradient (S × (t ≥ 1) interaction exp(coef) 1.12, p 0.87; PH test p 0.054). The signal predicts disposal at every horizon, not only the immediate one.",
  "block": "HR per 10 pp of the controlling block 0.964 [0.908, 1.024] conditional on S (p 0.23); unconditional KM: disposed within 5 years 0.76 (low block tercile) vs 0.58 (high). Consistent with the paper's reading that the block works through the signal."
